/* ================= t330 / t331 shops you can walk into. The owner: "These new restaurants and stores and workhands to be
   physical visual things you can see", "the staff you hire for stores should also be physical", "it shouldn't be stands, it
   should be stores; the stands are ugly and not well made", "when you upgrade stores you should see a visual difference
   exterior and interior".
   - MARKET ROW. The main road east of the Lamplighter is cleared into lots. Your own shop (a farm stand, a kitchen or a taproom)
     stands on the first one as a real building in the town's own style, with your shop's name over the door; in a versus
     world each player's shop has its own lot along the row. Each trade keeps its piece at the door from the start: a stand
     its crates of produce, a kitchen its menu board, a taproom its barrel.
   - INSIDE. Each trade has its own room and its own pieces: the stand its produce bins, egg crates and a scale on the
     counter; the kitchen its stove, a pass with the plates waiting under the heat shelf, and tables laid with plates; the
     taproom its bar with the taps, kegs, and tables with mugs. The people you hire work, each at a job that loops: the clerk
     weighs and bags, a hand carries crates in from the back, the cook stirs at the stove, another plates at the pass, the
     barman pulls pints at the taps, a waiter carries the tray out to the tables. Customers come in, look, order, sit and go.
   - UPGRADES SHOW. A painted sign: outside, the hand-lettered plank over the door becomes a painted board in the trade's
     colours with gilt letters and the trade's picture; inside, the chalk slate gives way to a painted price board, and the
     shop's name goes up on the wall over the counter. Longer hours: a lantern lit by the door by day and night, an OPEN
     board on the step and an OPEN sign on the door; inside, lit lanterns on the walls, warm light on the floor, an OPEN sign
     in the window and a lamp on the counter. A second line: an awning, the second trade's goods out front and its own piece
     inside (a basket table, a bake case, a cask bar). The back room: the building widens with two more windows the same size,
     and the room inside is half as big again.
   - THE TOWN'S SHOPS GROW TOO. A share's "building next door" is a second building down Market Row in the shop's own
     materials, name and front (Coyle's shop window and bread rack, Bell's barn door and sacks, the forge's anvil, Hartley's
     boards and sawhorse, the bait shop's cooler, the Lamplighter's lamp and bench, the inn's porch), and a branch in Wickham
     is a flat-fronted shop on Wickham's high street in the same colours (no more market stalls); the hands you hire them
     serve at the counter and stock the shelves.
   The buildings come from the same Aseprite building kit as the rest of the town (tools: t330/st30bld.lua); the shops' pieces
   are drawn by code in the furniture's own palette (t330/st30art.py). Both are packed below. === */
